<h2 id="outlook">What's Next for New York</h2>
<p>The Giants are 1-1 and now hand the offense to Winston for the foreseeable future, with the front office keeping "all options on the table" for added quarterback depth. Harbaugh didn't rule out a Dart return if New York makes a playoff push, but the more realistic timeline points to a full recovery well ahead of the 2027 season, when Dart is expected to resume his job as the franchise's starter.</p>
<div class="callout">
<strong>No Testing Numbers, Real Production</strong>
  Dart is proof that a combine data sheet isn't the only way to measure an athlete. He never ran a 40 or jumped for scouts — his college and rookie rushing numbers were always the evidence, and they were enough to make him a first-round pick and, briefly, a record-setter.
</div>
