<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">What injury did Jaxson Dart suffer?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Dart tore his left MCL and PCL and damaged his meniscus in Week 2 against the Los Angeles Rams. His ACL was not damaged, but he will require season-ending surgery.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Who is the Giants' starting quarterback now?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Jameis Winston takes over as New York's starter for the rest of the 2026 season, with Jake Haener promoted from the practice squad as his backup.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Will Jaxson Dart play again this season?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Dart is expected to miss the rest of the regular season. Head coach John Harbaugh did not rule out a possible return if the Giants make the playoffs, but Dart is more realistically expected back for the 2027 season.</div>
